1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:30,000
= kissasia.net =

2
00:01:47,586 --> 00:01:49,286
Go on.

3
00:01:49,286 --> 00:01:50,649
Boss.

4
00:01:50,649 --> 00:01:52,716
Anything you need me to do?

5
00:01:52,716 --> 00:01:54,141
Remember to eat on time.

6
00:01:54,141 --> 00:01:55,880
That's it?

7
00:01:55,880 --> 00:01:59,504
You're not even wishing me luck
on my promotion to captain?

8
00:01:59,504 --> 00:02:03,640
Something that is bound to happen
can't be called a prediction.

9
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:05,745
Then what about eating on time?

10
00:02:05,745 --> 00:02:08,450
Because you don't usually eat on time.

11
00:02:08,450 --> 00:02:09,450
I'm off.

12
00:02:16,727 --> 00:02:17,727
Good luck.

13
00:02:18,989 --> 00:02:20,038
See you.

14
00:02:20,720 --> 00:02:22,864
Mr. Fu, thanks for your hard work.

15
00:02:22,864 --> 00:02:24,084
Mentor.

16
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:26,599
I'm relieved you're here.

17
00:02:26,599 --> 00:02:30,110
I have a class today.
Just perform as you usually do.

18
00:02:32,245 --> 00:02:35,123
Ruan, remember this.

19
00:02:35,123 --> 00:02:37,307
You don't need everyone's approval.

20
00:02:37,307 --> 00:02:39,251
You don't need everyone's appreciation.

21
00:02:39,251 --> 00:02:41,436
You don't even need everyone's respect.

22
00:02:41,436 --> 00:02:44,307
But you must respect yourself.

23
00:02:44,307 --> 00:02:48,959
Exams like this will come up again and again
throughout your career.

24
00:02:48,959 --> 00:02:51,625
Don't fear them. Conquer them.

25
00:02:51,625 --> 00:02:53,780
- Good luck.
- I will, mentor.

26
00:03:04,267 --> 00:03:07,027
[Episode 19]
["Failure," Welcome Home!]

27
00:03:08,467 --> 00:03:10,162
I'll get going, instructor.

28
00:03:14,884 --> 00:03:17,381
You need to be cautious too.

29
00:03:17,381 --> 00:03:19,012
But you've done very well.

30
00:03:19,012 --> 00:03:22,507
Just do your best during the exam.
It should be fine.

31
00:03:22,507 --> 00:03:25,467
Time flies. You're about to be promoted to F7.

32
00:03:25,467 --> 00:03:28,627
Of all the pilots I know,
you've been promoted the fastest.

33
00:03:28,627 --> 00:03:30,147
Are you proud of me?

34
00:03:31,183 --> 00:03:32,841
You still need to be cautious.

35
00:03:32,841 --> 00:03:35,932
Be careful. The examiner
might give you a hard time.

36
00:03:35,932 --> 00:03:38,947
That's why I asked you to
go hard on me during the training.

37
00:03:38,947 --> 00:03:41,452
Don't worry about me.
I'm not afraid of anything.

38
00:03:41,452 --> 00:03:44,860
Worried about you? I was worried I'd throw up.

39
00:03:44,860 --> 00:03:46,719
Let's go eat.

40
00:03:47,307 --> 00:03:50,067
Mentor, I have a lunch date.

41
00:03:50,067 --> 00:03:53,347
Okay, I got it. A date with the boss.

42
00:03:53,347 --> 00:03:54,667
No.

43
00:03:54,667 --> 00:03:57,748
Actually, I've been so busy with exams lately.

44
00:03:57,748 --> 00:04:01,644
I've neglected him, but I'm not meeting him.
It's Jiang Zi Yue.

45
00:04:01,644 --> 00:04:04,223
Alright. Meet whoever you want.

46
00:04:04,223 --> 00:04:06,127
I'm going to eat.

47
00:04:06,127 --> 00:04:07,187
Goodbye, mentor.

48
00:04:07,187 --> 00:04:09,587
- Close the door.
- Okay.

49
00:04:09,587 --> 00:04:11,667
Anyway, I'm just giving you some advice.

50
00:04:11,667 --> 00:04:14,547
What you do with it is up to you.

51
00:04:15,368 --> 00:04:16,878
Thank you.

52
00:04:16,878 --> 00:04:18,533
I've already made up my mind.

53
00:04:23,650 --> 00:04:25,270
So there won't be a next time?

54
00:04:26,493 --> 00:04:29,917
You're speaking so loudly.
Not afraid of being heard anymore?

55
00:04:29,917 --> 00:04:32,267
Next time? Next time what?

56
00:04:32,267 --> 00:04:33,811
Next time we sleep together?

57
00:04:33,811 --> 00:04:34,811
Come on.

58
00:04:35,627 --> 00:04:37,542
Look how nervous you are.

59
00:04:39,067 --> 00:04:43,493
But seriously, I do hope
the next time you see me,

60
00:04:43,493 --> 00:04:44,638
you'll show me some respect.

61
00:04:44,638 --> 00:04:47,382
When have I not respected you, Jiang Zi Yue?

62
00:04:47,382 --> 00:04:49,648
The truth is,
you don't know what I really want.

63
00:04:49,648 --> 00:04:52,227
About my family,
I know I went too far last time.

64
00:04:52,227 --> 00:04:55,132
I hurt you, but... that's just who I am.

65
00:04:55,132 --> 00:04:57,547
I'd rather live in the moment
than think about the future.

66
00:04:57,547 --> 00:04:58,627
My happiness comes first.

67
00:04:58,627 --> 00:05:01,133
I don't want to waste time
explaining things to my family.

68
00:05:01,133 --> 00:05:04,278
And I don't want you to
have any illusions about us.

69
00:05:04,278 --> 00:05:07,467
So you're the one at fault, not me.
Your illusions are wrong.

70
00:05:07,467 --> 00:05:10,077
Of course, during this time without you...

71
00:05:12,598 --> 00:05:14,152
I was unhappy.

72
00:05:14,152 --> 00:05:15,926
I need you.

73
00:05:24,390 --> 00:05:26,295
"I need you."

74
00:05:26,295 --> 00:05:31,320
Do you know how long I've wanted to hear that?

75
00:05:31,320 --> 00:05:33,145
You're finally being honest.

76
00:05:33,145 --> 00:05:36,570
If you'd been this honest from the start,

77
00:05:36,570 --> 00:05:39,187
we wouldn't have ended up like this.

78
00:05:39,187 --> 00:05:43,492
What we had never needed to be hidden.

79
00:05:43,492 --> 00:05:45,317
Is it really me you need?

80
00:05:45,317 --> 00:05:48,879
What you need is a nanny,
a tool for your desires,

81
00:05:48,879 --> 00:05:52,517
someone at your beck and call,
nothing more than a pet.

82
00:06:01,587 --> 00:06:04,011
Yes, you're right.

83
00:06:04,947 --> 00:06:09,024
I'm selfish. I only care about
myself and my reputation.

84
00:06:09,827 --> 00:06:12,612
But I think it's instinctive.
I'm not in the wrong.

85
00:06:12,612 --> 00:06:14,787
You're the one who's wrong here.

86
00:06:14,787 --> 00:06:17,987
We agreed from the beginning that
this was how we would be together.

87
00:06:17,987 --> 00:06:20,171
But now, you've changed.

88
00:06:20,171 --> 00:06:22,907
I don't even know who turned you into this.

89
00:06:22,907 --> 00:06:26,227
Is it possible that I haven't changed at all?

90
00:06:26,227 --> 00:06:31,773
It's just that all this time,
you tried to make me into someone like you.

91
00:06:33,094 --> 00:06:36,464
Yes. Maybe you're not wrong.

92
00:06:36,464 --> 00:06:39,347
But now, I'm going to be myself.

93
00:06:39,347 --> 00:06:42,147
- Now you're talking about--
- Ms. Jiang.

94
00:06:42,147 --> 00:06:43,707
Ruan.

95
00:06:43,707 --> 00:06:45,591
Am I interrupting?

96
00:06:46,547 --> 00:06:49,651
No. We're finished talking. Let's go.

97
00:06:57,147 --> 00:06:59,693
Captain Yue Yang, goodbye.

98
00:06:59,693 --> 00:07:02,258
Captain Yue Yang, we're off to eat.

99
00:07:28,267 --> 00:07:30,240
[Jiang City]

100
00:07:42,765 --> 00:07:44,092
Thank you.

101
00:07:48,547 --> 00:07:50,059
Give me a hug.

102
00:08:01,812 --> 00:08:03,290
Thank you.

103
00:08:06,350 --> 00:08:07,658
Take care.

104
00:08:08,547 --> 00:08:09,884
I'm leaving.

105
00:09:19,534 --> 00:09:22,341
You didn't say you were coming.

106
00:09:22,341 --> 00:09:24,243
I was just passing by after work.

107
00:09:25,027 --> 00:09:28,461
That's quite a detour you've taken.

108
00:09:29,387 --> 00:09:31,816
Your studio looks nice.

109
00:09:32,638 --> 00:09:34,222
Do you want some instant noodles?

110
00:09:34,222 --> 00:09:37,127
I'm making some. I'll make you a bowl too.

111
00:09:37,127 --> 00:09:40,368
Is that okay? Living so frugally?

112
00:09:40,947 --> 00:09:43,011
It's not to save money.

113
00:09:43,011 --> 00:09:46,507
It's just that
this is the only thing I can cook.

114
00:09:46,507 --> 00:09:49,467
When Yan An was here,
he always ordered takeout.

115
00:09:49,467 --> 00:09:53,867
Now that he's gone,
it's hard to adjust to a simpler life.

116
00:09:53,867 --> 00:09:55,492
I'm not used to other takeout.

117
00:09:55,492 --> 00:09:57,796
And I can't bring myself to order
the same ones he did.

118
00:09:57,796 --> 00:09:59,022
They're too expensive.

119
00:09:59,022 --> 00:10:00,407
Look at you.

120
00:10:00,407 --> 00:10:04,121
You've been with Ms. Dong for years,
but you're nothing like her.

121
00:10:04,121 --> 00:10:06,067
She encourages me to be myself.

122
00:10:06,067 --> 00:10:09,427
She says our family doesn't need
another copy of anyone.

123
00:10:09,427 --> 00:10:11,772
But what's with you?

124
00:10:11,772 --> 00:10:14,529
You only call her "mom" when people are around.

125
00:10:18,347 --> 00:10:20,132
What if this is who I am?

126
00:10:20,132 --> 00:10:22,462
Then I'd look down on you.

127
00:10:22,462 --> 00:10:25,084
Ruan, that's a bit much.

128
00:10:29,947 --> 00:10:31,521
Let's add an egg.

129
00:10:33,772 --> 00:10:37,986
Every family has its problems, more or less.

130
00:10:37,986 --> 00:10:42,152
But you can't stay stuck in those problems
and trapped in that pain.

131
00:10:42,152 --> 00:10:44,267
Otherwise, you're making things
hard for yourself.

132
00:10:44,267 --> 00:10:47,707
Take me, for example.
I've been quite unhappy lately.

133
00:10:47,707 --> 00:10:50,533
My dad would rather trust an outsider than me.

134
00:10:50,533 --> 00:10:52,328
Who can I even complain to?

135
00:10:54,747 --> 00:10:57,292
I know you're trying to comfort me.

136
00:10:57,292 --> 00:11:01,827
I admit I acted out of spite
and hurt everyone that day.

137
00:11:01,827 --> 00:11:07,587
Honestly, I've been keeping up
with your social media for years.

138
00:11:07,587 --> 00:11:09,372
You like my work?

139
00:11:09,372 --> 00:11:10,593
To be honest...

140
00:11:11,406 --> 00:11:12,666
it's for her.

141
00:11:21,805 --> 00:11:23,480
Well...

142
00:11:25,023 --> 00:11:29,307
I've hogged your mom for so many years.
I guess I owe you.

143
00:11:29,307 --> 00:11:30,771
How about this?

144
00:11:30,771 --> 00:11:33,619
From now on, I'll be twice as good to you.

145
00:11:33,619 --> 00:11:35,107
Then we'll be even.

146
00:11:35,107 --> 00:11:39,231
Can you accept this awful sister
who embarrassed your family?

147
00:11:39,878 --> 00:11:41,418
Actually...

148
00:11:42,612 --> 00:11:45,107
when I was fourteen,

149
00:11:45,107 --> 00:11:48,052
I was already ready to have a sister.

150
00:11:48,052 --> 00:11:49,716
You're just late.

151
00:11:49,716 --> 00:11:50,897
Sister.

152
00:12:05,946 --> 00:12:09,068
Alright. I'm hungry.
Go make some instant noodles.

153
00:12:09,068 --> 00:12:10,763
Okay.

154
00:12:11,518 --> 00:12:13,658
The noodles are almost ready anyway.

155
00:12:37,147 --> 00:12:41,161
I took these portraits during the opening.

156
00:12:43,199 --> 00:12:45,504
This person is...?

157
00:12:45,504 --> 00:12:46,889
Uncle Guo.

158
00:12:46,889 --> 00:12:49,487
He's Mom's good friend. You don't know him?

159
00:12:49,487 --> 00:12:52,152
No. I don't remember seeing him that day.

160
00:12:52,152 --> 00:12:54,851
That's understandable. He was busy that day.

161
00:12:54,851 --> 00:12:57,221
By the time he arrived, you'd already left.

162
00:12:58,145 --> 00:13:02,787
Did you say they're friends?

163
00:13:02,787 --> 00:13:04,747
He used to be Mom's manager.

164
00:13:04,747 --> 00:13:06,947
He's also something of a matchmaker.

165
00:13:06,947 --> 00:13:12,536
When Ms. Dong's career started to take off,
he introduced my dad and mom.

166
00:13:15,061 --> 00:13:18,627
The noodles are about done.
Want some green onions?

167
00:13:20,107 --> 00:13:23,052
I'm not eating.
I remembered I have something to do.

168
00:13:23,052 --> 00:13:26,107
Wait. Sister, I cooked two portions.

169
00:13:26,107 --> 00:13:30,143
If you don't eat,
how can I finish it all by myself?

170
00:13:33,960 --> 00:13:37,440
[Mingchen Residences]

171
00:14:26,270 --> 00:14:28,061
Happy fifth anniversary.

172
00:14:30,238 --> 00:14:34,102
Why didn't you remind me that
today was our fifth anniversary?

173
00:14:34,102 --> 00:14:36,672
You said you wanted to be alone today.

174
00:14:36,672 --> 00:14:40,097
If I had brought it up,
wouldn't that be inconsiderate?

175
00:14:40,097 --> 00:14:43,283
But I even forgot our fifth anniversary.
Aren't you mad?

176
00:14:43,283 --> 00:14:46,587
An anniversary is just an ordinary day.

177
00:14:46,587 --> 00:14:49,412
What matters more
is the time we've spent together.

178
00:14:49,412 --> 00:14:52,718
We've created countless memories
worth holding on to.

179
00:14:52,718 --> 00:14:57,703
Getting upset just because you forgot
an anniversary feels so backwards.

180
00:14:57,703 --> 00:15:01,289
Letting one bad moment
erase all our happy memories?

181
00:15:01,289 --> 00:15:03,067
I don't think that's right.

182
00:15:03,067 --> 00:15:05,940
So, as long as I remember it, that's enough.

183
00:15:09,122 --> 00:15:13,367
Mr. Fu, you're so thorough. Not a single flaw.

184
00:15:14,067 --> 00:15:15,491
But what if you forget?

185
00:15:15,491 --> 00:15:20,467
The day I won you over means so much to me.

186
00:15:20,467 --> 00:15:22,357
I could never forget it.

187
00:15:31,984 --> 00:15:33,766
I'm sorry.

188
00:15:33,766 --> 00:15:37,507
Lately, I've been neglecting you a bit.

189
00:15:39,347 --> 00:15:41,401
Why are you apologizing?

190
00:15:42,147 --> 00:15:44,260
As the boyfriend of a pilot,

191
00:15:44,867 --> 00:15:48,787
I understand, and I want to support you.

192
00:15:48,787 --> 00:15:52,401
Also, it hurts me to see you working so hard.

193
00:15:53,467 --> 00:15:54,542
Try some.

194
00:15:55,347 --> 00:15:56,784
Take a big bite.

195
00:15:59,894 --> 00:16:01,554
Do you feel a bit better now?

196
00:16:02,918 --> 00:16:05,827
Or do you want to tell me about it?

197
00:16:05,827 --> 00:16:07,652
I don't want to burden you with it.

198
00:16:07,652 --> 00:16:09,557
Now you're being a stranger.

199
00:16:09,557 --> 00:16:14,338
I'm your friend first, boyfriend second.

200
00:16:14,338 --> 00:16:16,247
Who's your friend?

201
00:16:17,011 --> 00:16:19,756
I remember one night. It was raining very hard.

202
00:16:19,756 --> 00:16:22,987
Your mom asked me what our relationship was.

203
00:16:22,987 --> 00:16:24,765
I said we were friends.

204
00:16:24,765 --> 00:16:27,347
And you said, "Yes, we're friends."

205
00:16:27,347 --> 00:16:30,214
What? Are you trying to deny it now?

206
00:16:32,847 --> 00:16:34,426
Listen, Ms. Ruan.

207
00:16:35,267 --> 00:16:40,147
Besides being the closest of lovers,
we are also each other's best friends.

208
00:16:40,147 --> 00:16:44,722
No matter your mood,
good or bad, I'll take it all.

209
00:16:50,594 --> 00:16:54,758
So I think you should give You An a chance.

210
00:16:59,382 --> 00:17:00,887
You An, you're back.

211
00:17:00,887 --> 00:17:02,591
Why are you here?

212
00:17:02,591 --> 00:17:05,079
Never mind. I don't want to know.

213
00:17:07,907 --> 00:17:10,899
Well, Mr. Zheng, Ms. Dong, I'll be going now.

214
00:17:11,507 --> 00:17:12,848
Leaving already?

215
00:17:12,848 --> 00:17:14,227
Yan An.

216
00:17:15,267 --> 00:17:17,133
Thank you for what you said today.

217
00:17:17,133 --> 00:17:19,757
- I'll come by again.
- Okay, get home safely.

218
00:17:19,757 --> 00:17:20,757
Will do.

219
00:17:43,936 --> 00:17:45,458
You An.

220
00:17:46,886 --> 00:17:48,911
Why are the lights off?

221
00:17:48,911 --> 00:17:51,271
I can't find something.

222
00:17:51,271 --> 00:17:53,010
What are you looking for?

223
00:17:55,587 --> 00:17:58,018
It's not important. What is it?

224
00:17:58,827 --> 00:18:02,044
Your dad and I want to talk with you.

225
00:18:05,126 --> 00:18:06,831
About what?

226
00:18:06,831 --> 00:18:10,336
What would he and I even have to talk about?

227
00:18:10,336 --> 00:18:12,601
I know you've felt wronged lately.

228
00:18:12,601 --> 00:18:14,587
Your dad told me everything.

229
00:18:14,587 --> 00:18:18,107
But I think you may have misunderstood him.

230
00:18:18,107 --> 00:18:20,547
I misunderstood him?

231
00:18:20,547 --> 00:18:24,307
He made it perfectly clear.

232
00:18:24,307 --> 00:18:25,931
I'm a girl.

233
00:18:25,931 --> 00:18:30,804
My mission in this family
is to find him a good son-in-law.

234
00:18:31,707 --> 00:18:33,772
It seems you're still angry.

235
00:18:33,772 --> 00:18:36,663
When a person is angry,
it's not a good time to talk business.

236
00:18:36,663 --> 00:18:38,442
Let's talk another day.

237
00:18:39,193 --> 00:18:40,885
What business?

238
00:18:41,862 --> 00:18:47,347
Your dad has decided to hand over
the Jiang City Airport Hotel to you.

239
00:18:47,347 --> 00:18:48,507
Really?

240
00:18:48,507 --> 00:18:50,373
Why would I lie about that?

241
00:18:50,373 --> 00:18:53,547
But... you seem quite tired today.

242
00:18:53,547 --> 00:18:56,831
Forget it. Let's talk another day.
Get some rest.

243
00:18:56,831 --> 00:18:59,507
Mom, I'm not tired at all. I can talk.

244
00:18:59,507 --> 00:19:01,688
Come in, let's have a good talk.

245
00:19:06,307 --> 00:19:07,569
Dad.

246
00:19:12,987 --> 00:19:18,308
If you've misunderstood someone for years,
how do you face them?

247
00:19:18,308 --> 00:19:20,437
Why bring this up all of a sudden?

248
00:19:22,907 --> 00:19:25,412
Haven't we moved on from that topic?

249
00:19:25,412 --> 00:19:27,837
Why are you so nervous?

250
00:19:27,837 --> 00:19:31,984
You have experience with this,
so I wanted your advice.

251
00:19:33,107 --> 00:19:34,493
Then...

252
00:19:35,427 --> 00:19:37,296
who did you misunderstand?

253
00:19:39,308 --> 00:19:40,920
My mom.

254
00:19:42,467 --> 00:19:48,047
All these years,
I've been forcing myself to hate her.

255
00:19:49,307 --> 00:19:53,839
But then I realized... I was wrong.

256
00:19:54,429 --> 00:19:56,147
I was terribly wrong.

257
00:20:04,901 --> 00:20:07,021
What exactly happened?

258
00:20:07,987 --> 00:20:09,614
Tell me about it.

259
00:20:12,205 --> 00:20:14,026
I don't want to talk about it.

260
00:20:16,707 --> 00:20:18,259
Let me think.

261
00:20:19,247 --> 00:20:23,937
When I realized I had misunderstood you,
how did I deal with it?

262
00:20:26,907 --> 00:20:29,189
It didn't seem that hard.

263
00:20:29,189 --> 00:20:32,199
Because at that time,
I wanted to see you so badly.

264
00:20:32,867 --> 00:20:35,012
So naturally, I had to face it.

265
00:20:55,829 --> 00:20:58,571
You An, you should know,

266
00:20:58,571 --> 00:21:02,347
you are my daughter and my whole world.

267
00:21:02,347 --> 00:21:07,051
Mr. Zheng, are you here to
talk about feelings or business?

268
00:21:07,051 --> 00:21:09,036
Can we get to the point?

269
00:21:09,036 --> 00:21:13,851
You An. Your dad always talks about
feelings first, then business.

270
00:21:14,525 --> 00:21:15,827
Exactly.

271
00:21:15,827 --> 00:21:18,062
Your mom knows me best.

272
00:21:20,623 --> 00:21:22,587
- Where was I?
- Whole world.

273
00:21:22,587 --> 00:21:23,587
Right.

274
00:21:25,846 --> 00:21:27,126
You An.

275
00:21:28,295 --> 00:21:31,267
You're my only daughter.

276
00:21:31,267 --> 00:21:33,452
You're my everything.

277
00:21:33,452 --> 00:21:35,638
Everything I have will be yours.

278
00:21:35,638 --> 00:21:37,947
I won't give it to anyone else.

279
00:21:37,947 --> 00:21:40,892
You're a princess to me.

280
00:21:40,892 --> 00:21:43,147
I won't let my princess

281
00:21:43,147 --> 00:21:49,552
suffer even a bit of grievance
or bear any pressure.

282
00:21:55,267 --> 00:21:58,477
Dad, you know it too.

283
00:21:58,477 --> 00:22:00,813
You can't protect me forever.

284
00:22:00,813 --> 00:22:03,452
Even if you want to find yourself a successor,

285
00:22:03,452 --> 00:22:05,798
what if you trust the wrong person?

286
00:22:05,798 --> 00:22:07,702
I'm an adult now.

287
00:22:07,702 --> 00:22:13,132
I'm way past... wanting to be a princess.

288
00:22:13,132 --> 00:22:15,827
You can protect me and love me.

289
00:22:15,827 --> 00:22:22,187
But shouldn't you be teaching me
how to fight and survive in the real world,

290
00:22:22,187 --> 00:22:25,421
instead of taking away my sword
and locking me in a tower?

291
00:22:25,421 --> 00:22:30,921
You can't say you love me
while stripping me of my rights and my freedom.

292
00:22:30,921 --> 00:22:32,627
Look at her.

293
00:22:32,627 --> 00:22:36,573
I say one thing,
and she has a dozen arguments ready.

294
00:22:40,788 --> 00:22:44,267
Look. I won't hand over
all my businesses to you.

295
00:22:44,267 --> 00:22:48,772
That would be unfair to you,
me, or the company.

296
00:22:48,772 --> 00:22:55,674
You have to understand,
behind every employee is a family like ours.

297
00:22:56,347 --> 00:22:58,247
So I've decided to start

298
00:22:59,307 --> 00:23:04,133
by putting the Jiang City Airport Hotel
entirely in your hands.

299
00:23:04,133 --> 00:23:06,566
Don't celebrate too soon.

300
00:23:07,907 --> 00:23:10,347
You'll be responsible for profits and losses.

301
00:23:10,347 --> 00:23:13,427
I won't lift a finger to help you.

302
00:23:13,427 --> 00:23:19,109
I want you to know how hard it was for me.

303
00:23:21,080 --> 00:23:22,381
Of course.

304
00:23:23,147 --> 00:23:25,089
If you feel too much pressure,

305
00:23:25,089 --> 00:23:30,306
or if managing a hotel is too--

306
00:23:30,306 --> 00:23:34,321
Mr. Zheng. Then we have a deal.

307
00:23:35,652 --> 00:23:39,767
You're that confident, Ms. Zheng?

308
00:23:43,494 --> 00:23:46,600
Bosses, are you done with business?

309
00:23:46,600 --> 00:23:49,744
Please, sit. I have something to say too.

310
00:23:49,744 --> 00:23:51,103
Yes.

311
00:23:52,990 --> 00:23:58,215
You An, you should thank
Yan An properly this time.

312
00:23:58,215 --> 00:24:01,520
If Yan An hadn't told us,
we'd never have known how you felt.

313
00:24:01,520 --> 00:24:05,135
- Exactly.
- You never talked to us about these things.

314
00:24:06,454 --> 00:24:08,307
Yan An?

315
00:24:08,307 --> 00:24:11,767
Since the last gathering,
he's been trying to persuade your dad.

316
00:24:11,767 --> 00:24:13,633
He even put in a good word for you.

317
00:24:13,633 --> 00:24:16,138
Was how you treated him just now appropriate?

318
00:24:16,138 --> 00:24:17,527
Exactly.

319
00:24:19,038 --> 00:24:21,507
He... He owes me.

320
00:24:21,507 --> 00:24:25,292
My child, it's not about whether he owes you.

321
00:24:25,292 --> 00:24:28,029
It's only about whether he wants to.

322
00:24:31,775 --> 00:24:33,387
I understand.

323
00:24:40,767 --> 00:24:44,446
Ruan. You must be quite nervous.

324
00:24:44,446 --> 00:24:46,875
To have made it to the left-seat exam.

325
00:24:47,547 --> 00:24:50,408
But I have to make it clear.

326
00:24:50,408 --> 00:24:53,787
I treat every pilot equally,
whether they're men or women.

327
00:24:53,787 --> 00:24:58,911
So if you find the exam difficult later,
it's nothing personal.

328
00:25:02,911 --> 00:25:04,376
Instructor Yue.

329
00:25:04,376 --> 00:25:09,507
We've all earned our places
through medicals and assessments.

330
00:25:09,507 --> 00:25:12,722
So I hope that
you won't go easy on me on the exam.

331
00:25:12,722 --> 00:25:15,563
Good. Prove yourself with your actions.

332
00:25:25,667 --> 00:25:31,667
[Severe Turbulence: 80% Intensity]

333
00:25:31,667 --> 00:25:36,547
[Moderate Icing]

334
00:25:36,547 --> 00:25:40,767
[Heavy Rain &amp; Strong Crosswind]

335
00:25:43,627 --> 00:25:45,100
1,000.

336
00:25:49,747 --> 00:25:51,866
- Category III.
- Checked.

337
00:25:51,866 --> 00:25:53,626
- Category I.
- Checked.

338
00:25:53,626 --> 00:25:55,116
Wipers on.

339
00:25:58,108 --> 00:26:00,084
Above 100. Minimums.

340
00:26:01,492 --> 00:26:02,616
Checked.

341
00:26:03,771 --> 00:26:05,507
Continue.

342
00:26:05,507 --> 00:26:07,491
Visual reference.

343
00:26:31,787 --> 00:26:33,178
100.

344
00:26:35,587 --> 00:26:36,787
50.

345
00:26:36,787 --> 00:26:37,906
40.

346
00:26:37,906 --> 00:26:38,987
30.

347
00:26:38,987 --> 00:26:39,898
20.

348
00:26:39,898 --> 00:26:41,381
Retard.

349
00:27:02,734 --> 00:27:04,337
[Left Turn Practice Exam]

350
00:27:04,337 --> 00:27:06,357
Attention, crew. Take your positions.

351
00:27:06,357 --> 00:27:08,987
[Failed]
[Reason: Runway Excursion]

352
00:27:34,502 --> 00:27:36,427
Ruan.

353
00:27:36,427 --> 00:27:38,202
Is the exam over?

354
00:27:46,908 --> 00:27:48,146
Instructor Yue.

355
00:27:48,146 --> 00:27:49,507
Instructor Fan.

356
00:27:49,507 --> 00:27:51,205
Good work.

357
00:27:51,827 --> 00:27:55,894
What's the situation?
That was fast. It doesn't look good.

358
00:27:55,894 --> 00:27:57,121
It doesn't.

359
00:27:57,121 --> 00:28:00,113
Her result is a bit disappointing.

360
00:28:00,113 --> 00:28:02,586
How could that be?
She usually performs well in practice.

361
00:28:02,586 --> 00:28:04,707
Where did it go wrong?

362
00:28:04,707 --> 00:28:07,787
Maybe her fundamentals aren't solid enough.

363
00:28:07,787 --> 00:28:10,415
If you put it that way,
I guess the problem is with me.

364
00:28:10,415 --> 00:28:14,174
Instructor Fan, that's not what I meant. Truly.

365
00:28:14,867 --> 00:28:17,172
I want to see where the problem was.

366
00:28:17,172 --> 00:28:18,787
Can we review the footage?

367
00:28:18,787 --> 00:28:20,467
- Now?
- Yes.

368
00:28:20,467 --> 00:28:21,973
Let's take a look.

369
00:28:23,587 --> 00:28:24,871
- Don't you have work to do?
- Yes.

370
00:28:24,871 --> 00:28:26,787
Show her the footage after that.

371
00:28:26,787 --> 00:28:29,332
Captain Yue, we're in the next group together.

372
00:28:29,332 --> 00:28:31,957
An hour from now. We've got time.

373
00:28:31,957 --> 00:28:33,067
Let's review it now.

374
00:28:33,067 --> 00:28:35,692
Ruan, come in. See where the problem was.

375
00:28:35,692 --> 00:28:38,124
You usually practice so well.
What's with you today?

376
00:28:38,124 --> 00:28:40,388
You must be nervous and hasty.

377
00:28:40,388 --> 00:28:41,972
Shall we?

378
00:28:41,972 --> 00:28:45,058
- Okay. Play it.
- Okay.

379
00:28:45,058 --> 00:28:47,307
Sit, please.

380
00:28:47,307 --> 00:28:49,623
- Thank you.
- No problem.

381
00:28:54,037 --> 00:28:56,312
Can you see from where you're sitting?

382
00:28:57,587 --> 00:29:00,467
Instructor Fan, I have a meeting to attend.

383
00:29:00,467 --> 00:29:02,103
Take your time watching.

384
00:29:13,837 --> 00:29:15,337
Wipers on.

385
00:29:34,230 --> 00:29:35,532
Go on.

386
00:29:50,701 --> 00:29:52,625
That's all of it, Instructor Fan.

387
00:29:52,625 --> 00:29:54,187
Any instructions?

388
00:29:54,187 --> 00:29:56,625
You flatter me. I'm just learning.

389
00:29:56,625 --> 00:29:58,987
Captain Yue, you're really very strict.

390
00:29:58,987 --> 00:30:00,467
How so?

391
00:30:00,467 --> 00:30:02,547
Look at the test you designed.

392
00:30:02,547 --> 00:30:05,907
You added so many complicated emergencies.

393
00:30:05,907 --> 00:30:10,776
If I were on that plane,
I wouldn't have reacted in time.

394
00:30:10,776 --> 00:30:12,547
- Is that so?
- Absolutely.

395
00:30:12,547 --> 00:30:15,052
But it's good for the trainees.

396
00:30:15,052 --> 00:30:19,023
If they ever encounter this in the future,
they'll know how to handle it.

397
00:30:19,023 --> 00:30:22,067
But, Instructor Fan, let me explain this.

398
00:30:22,067 --> 00:30:26,027
I did all this because she's your trainee.

399
00:30:26,027 --> 00:30:29,732
I genuinely hope she can become a pilot
as good as you.

400
00:30:29,732 --> 00:30:32,559
So I hold her to a higher standard.

401
00:30:32,559 --> 00:30:33,947
- As it should be.
- Right?

402
00:30:33,947 --> 00:30:37,566
Every pilot should be held to such a standard.

403
00:30:37,566 --> 00:30:39,111
I'll make a note of that.

404
00:30:39,111 --> 00:30:42,463
I've really learned a lot from you today.

405
00:30:43,467 --> 00:30:45,412
And Ruan, you must remember this.

406
00:30:45,412 --> 00:30:49,638
As pilots, we are responsible for
all the passengers' safety on board.

407
00:30:49,638 --> 00:30:54,143
So we must go through
all sorts of rigorous trials.

408
00:30:54,143 --> 00:30:57,433
- Exactly. Well said.
- It's nothing personal.

409
00:30:57,433 --> 00:31:00,747
Why don't you two stay here and chat?
I'll go get ready.

410
00:31:00,747 --> 00:31:02,895
Captain Yue, what's the rush?

411
00:31:02,895 --> 00:31:05,347
We'll do the next group together.

412
00:31:05,347 --> 00:31:06,467
How about this?

413
00:31:06,467 --> 00:31:11,347
Just as you said, for the trainees' sake
and for the passengers' safety,

414
00:31:11,347 --> 00:31:13,491
we'll stick to the same standard later.

415
00:31:13,491 --> 00:31:15,240
What do you think?

416
00:31:15,240 --> 00:31:17,411
The same... standard?

417
00:31:17,411 --> 00:31:18,411
Yes.

418
00:31:47,987 --> 00:31:49,427
Four reds.

419
00:31:52,067 --> 00:31:54,157
Attention, crew. Take your positions.

420
00:31:54,157 --> 00:31:56,747
[Failed]
[Reason: Short Landing]

421
00:32:19,474 --> 00:32:20,943
100.

422
00:32:22,521 --> 00:32:23,747
50.

423
00:32:23,747 --> 00:32:24,826
40.

424
00:32:24,826 --> 00:32:25,947
30.

425
00:32:25,947 --> 00:32:26,947
20.

426
00:32:29,337 --> 00:32:30,447
Retard.

427
00:32:34,657 --> 00:32:35,666
[Failed]

428
00:32:35,666 --> 00:32:38,673
[Reason: Runway Excursion]
Attention, crew. Take your positions.

429
00:33:18,907 --> 00:33:21,919
Alright, don't look so dejected. It happens.

430
00:33:21,919 --> 00:33:25,328
The company only has a few slots each year.
It's not easy to become a captain.

431
00:33:25,328 --> 00:33:26,823
Keep working. You'll have another chance.

432
00:33:26,823 --> 00:33:29,747
It's normal for Captain Yue to be strict.

433
00:33:29,747 --> 00:33:32,073
Alright. Go home and reflect on it.

434
00:33:38,441 --> 00:33:40,007
Mentor.

435
00:33:41,095 --> 00:33:43,162
You can stop pretending.

436
00:33:44,315 --> 00:33:46,230
You're amazing, mentor.

437
00:33:48,067 --> 00:33:49,947
I was feeling pretty bad at first.

438
00:33:49,947 --> 00:33:52,772
I've practiced day and night for this.

439
00:33:52,772 --> 00:33:54,358
Who hasn't been there?

440
00:33:54,358 --> 00:33:58,077
What pilot doesn't have nightmares about exams?

441
00:33:59,187 --> 00:34:01,067
Failure may not be a bad thing.

442
00:34:01,067 --> 00:34:02,507
You can hone your skills more.

443
00:34:02,507 --> 00:34:07,067
Getting a shot at the left-seat test this fast
is bound to invite jealousy.

444
00:34:07,067 --> 00:34:10,227
Sometimes, moving too fast isn't a good thing.

445
00:34:10,227 --> 00:34:12,307
I know that myself.

446
00:34:12,307 --> 00:34:15,932
Getting straight to the line
is like a head start.

447
00:34:15,932 --> 00:34:18,467
That's bound to spark some envy, you know.

448
00:34:18,467 --> 00:34:21,492
Getting the left seat isn't a lifetime pass.

449
00:34:21,492 --> 00:34:24,077
You'll still face
all kinds of exams every year.

450
00:34:24,077 --> 00:34:25,587
Haven't you heard?

451
00:34:25,587 --> 00:34:30,692
- Being a co-pilot is the best value for money.
- I know.

452
00:34:30,692 --> 00:34:32,398
Where are you going? I'll give you a ride.

453
00:34:32,398 --> 00:34:34,142
No, thanks. I've called a ride.

454
00:34:34,142 --> 00:34:37,627
I'm going to a friend's bar later to celebrate.

455
00:34:37,627 --> 00:34:41,487
With that mindset, you'll pass sooner or later.

456
00:34:42,053 --> 00:34:44,779
- I'm off.
- Okay. Goodbye, mentor.

457
00:34:48,309 --> 00:34:51,866
Since you didn't pass,
are we still celebrating?

458
00:34:51,866 --> 00:34:54,034
There isn't much to celebrate.

459
00:34:54,603 --> 00:34:57,707
But you know what? I'm actually in a good mood.

460
00:34:57,707 --> 00:35:01,691
Ruan, what got on you?

461
00:35:01,691 --> 00:35:04,507
No, I'm really in a good mood.

462
00:35:04,507 --> 00:35:08,052
In fact, the more I think about failing,
the more at ease I feel.

463
00:35:08,052 --> 00:35:11,732
We barely started drinking,
and you're already talking drunk.

464
00:35:11,732 --> 00:35:15,787
You know that ever since I joined Hengshi Air,

465
00:35:15,787 --> 00:35:18,772
the gossip about me has never stopped.

466
00:35:18,772 --> 00:35:22,675
Sometimes I felt like I didn't even
start from the same line as them.

467
00:35:22,675 --> 00:35:24,419
I acted like I didn't care,

468
00:35:24,419 --> 00:35:28,102
but deep down,
I still wanted everyone's recognition.

469
00:35:28,102 --> 00:35:32,267
So I forced myself not to fail.

470
00:35:32,267 --> 00:35:36,277
The result was that I was exhausted.

471
00:35:36,277 --> 00:35:37,879
Okay.

472
00:35:37,879 --> 00:35:39,543
Go on.

473
00:35:39,543 --> 00:35:44,534
Although I failed this time,
at least I was treated fairly.

474
00:35:44,534 --> 00:35:46,680
Everyone's starting point is the same again.

475
00:35:46,680 --> 00:35:49,949
They don't have to be jealous of me
for having a boyfriend like Fu Ming Yu.

476
00:35:49,949 --> 00:35:53,255
Even with him as my boyfriend,
if I fail, I fail.

477
00:35:53,255 --> 00:35:56,907
That makes things much simpler.
If I'm not good enough, I'll practice more.

478
00:35:56,907 --> 00:36:00,507
I've finally stripped away
all the labels attached to me.

479
00:36:00,507 --> 00:36:03,652
I don't have to care about
how others judge me anymore.

480
00:36:03,652 --> 00:36:05,707
Now I feel so relieved.

481
00:36:05,707 --> 00:36:09,267
I still wish you'd passed
while the others failed.

482
00:36:09,267 --> 00:36:10,715
I'd be more satisfied.

483
00:36:11,381 --> 00:36:15,397
Those guys were quite unlucky.

484
00:36:15,397 --> 00:36:16,742
They took the test with me.

485
00:36:16,742 --> 00:36:19,606
Otherwise, at least
one of them would've passed.

486
00:36:19,606 --> 00:36:23,227
That's life.
You can't always get what you want.

487
00:36:23,227 --> 00:36:26,372
I thought returning to Hengshi Air
would be my big comeback.

488
00:36:26,372 --> 00:36:30,249
But now I realize
everything follows its natural course.

489
00:36:30,249 --> 00:36:33,954
If you don't deserve the seat,
you'll pay the price.

490
00:36:33,954 --> 00:36:35,419
Are you really okay?

491
00:36:35,419 --> 00:36:38,147
I'm really fine. I'm not a child.

492
00:36:38,147 --> 00:36:40,453
This little setback isn't going to break me.

493
00:36:40,453 --> 00:36:44,692
Okay. Then, raise your glasses, girls.

494
00:36:44,692 --> 00:36:49,375
Because of your exam,
it's been so long since we all got together.

495
00:36:50,027 --> 00:36:53,132
I'll toast to failure.

496
00:36:53,132 --> 00:36:56,438
Failure's mother opened the door for failure.

497
00:36:56,438 --> 00:36:59,662
And she said, "Welcome home."

498
00:36:59,662 --> 00:37:03,513
- Welcome home! Cheers!
- Welcome home! Cheers!

499
00:37:08,101 --> 00:37:10,006
Dong, play us a song.

500
00:37:10,006 --> 00:37:11,278
You got it!

501
00:37:30,514 --> 00:37:31,813
That's right.

502
00:37:31,813 --> 00:37:36,152
Failure's mother never asks her son
why he failed.

503
00:37:36,957 --> 00:37:39,886
She only hopes he'll come home early.

504
00:37:40,787 --> 00:37:43,309
Go ahead and mess something up.

505
00:37:43,309 --> 00:37:47,733
Then you'll find out that
the earth is still spinning.

506
00:37:48,653 --> 00:37:53,287
You don't have to be perfect
to be loved by your family and friends.

507
00:37:54,493 --> 00:37:56,078
Go ahead and embrace failure.

508
00:37:56,078 --> 00:37:58,683
Fifty-fifty is pretty good odds.

509
00:37:59,437 --> 00:38:03,744
See the world from the perspective
of who didn't win.

510
00:38:05,093 --> 00:38:09,787
Truly accept your own ordinariness
and take control of your life.

511
00:38:09,787 --> 00:38:15,091
So, my dear friend,
please be generous with life.

512
00:38:15,091 --> 00:38:18,298
Let things happen.

513
00:38:46,668 --> 00:38:49,638
Why are you stopping me?
This shouldn't have happened at Hengshi Air.

514
00:38:49,638 --> 00:38:51,667
You have to let things happen.

515
00:38:51,667 --> 00:38:53,948
Exams always come
with a chance of passing or failing.

516
00:38:53,948 --> 00:38:56,027
This isn't about passing or failing.

517
00:38:56,027 --> 00:38:58,958
- It's that you were targeted.
- It's normal to be targeted.

518
00:38:58,958 --> 00:39:00,863
There are only a few slots every year.

519
00:39:00,863 --> 00:39:02,867
If it wasn't me, it would've been someone else.

520
00:39:02,867 --> 00:39:05,136
That means our system has a serious problem.

521
00:39:05,136 --> 00:39:07,587
Employees don't have a fair path for promotion.

522
00:39:07,587 --> 00:39:10,132
Every year, they're exhausted
by all kinds of exams.

523
00:39:10,132 --> 00:39:15,092
- What's the point?
- To maintain a high priority on flight safety.

524
00:39:15,092 --> 00:39:17,712
It's an essential part of being a pilot.

525
00:39:17,712 --> 00:39:19,885
You want to argue with him over that?

526
00:39:19,885 --> 00:39:22,158
People would think I'm a sore loser.

527
00:39:24,813 --> 00:39:27,029
But you're unhappy.

528
00:39:27,029 --> 00:39:28,375
And I can't stand that.

529
00:39:28,375 --> 00:39:30,945
I'm not unhappy. I'm actually very happy.

530
00:39:30,945 --> 00:39:35,196
I used to be unhappy because everyone
assumed I only succeeded because of you.

531
00:39:35,196 --> 00:39:38,674
Now that rumor is debunked.
I couldn't be happier.

532
00:39:44,000 --> 00:39:45,340
Is that so?

533
00:39:46,462 --> 00:39:50,693
Actually, I didn't say
I was going to argue with him.

534
00:39:50,693 --> 00:39:52,371
You don't have to stop me.

535
00:39:53,094 --> 00:39:54,280
Then where are you going?

536
00:39:54,280 --> 00:39:57,227
I'm going to the restroom.

537
00:39:57,227 --> 00:39:58,734
Want to come along?

538
00:40:01,774 --> 00:40:05,055
Good attitude. Keep it up.

539
00:40:09,347 --> 00:40:11,987
- I'll go with you--
- Mr. Bai.

540
00:40:11,987 --> 00:40:13,364
Hold on.

541
00:40:15,997 --> 00:40:17,437
Come here.

542
00:40:21,028 --> 00:40:22,853
A bit closer.

543
00:40:25,695 --> 00:40:27,639
Didn't you say he was furious?

544
00:40:27,639 --> 00:40:28,997
Yes.

545
00:40:28,997 --> 00:40:31,507
You saw it just now. Mr. Fu was really angry.

546
00:40:31,507 --> 00:40:35,453
Didn't you also say he was going to
demand an explanation from Yue Yang?

547
00:40:35,453 --> 00:40:38,942
He said he'd stand up for you.

548
00:40:38,942 --> 00:40:41,648
But I don't know why he didn't--

549
00:40:41,648 --> 00:40:43,833
Is your intelligence even reliable?

550
00:40:43,833 --> 00:40:45,537
You can't even read your boss.

551
00:40:45,537 --> 00:40:48,723
I feel like I'm actually accurate
most of the time.

552
00:40:48,723 --> 00:40:52,147
But I can't help that
men are all cunning and fickle.

553
00:40:52,147 --> 00:40:53,647
Except for me, of course.

554
00:40:54,656 --> 00:40:57,507
Alright. I'm leaving.
I have a meeting to attend.

555
00:40:57,507 --> 00:40:58,888
Take care.

556
00:41:00,240 --> 00:41:02,917
Bye. Take care.

557
00:41:11,147 --> 00:41:14,547
- What's going on?
- You... This...

558
00:41:16,030 --> 00:41:17,656
It seems she's really fine.

559
00:41:17,656 --> 00:41:21,201
Mr. Fu, can't you ask her yourself after work?

560
00:41:21,201 --> 00:41:23,027
You don't know her.

561
00:41:23,027 --> 00:41:25,747
She won't say if something's on her mind.

562
00:41:25,747 --> 00:41:30,147
But if you want to test her next time,
could you please not sacrifice me?

563
00:41:30,147 --> 00:41:32,787
- I was asking you to play along.
- Is that so?

564
00:41:32,787 --> 00:41:35,611
How could I sacrifice you?

565
00:41:35,611 --> 00:41:38,067
You're my right-hand man.

566
00:41:38,067 --> 00:41:39,510
And my biggest headache.

567
00:41:41,863 --> 00:41:44,051
Look at this place.

568
00:41:44,051 --> 00:41:47,839
It has good bones, but why is it so run-down?

569
00:41:47,839 --> 00:41:49,667
Old is good.

570
00:41:49,667 --> 00:41:53,131
It gives me room for renovation.

571
00:41:53,131 --> 00:41:54,587
True.

572
00:41:54,587 --> 00:41:58,693
The potential is limitless,
but your budget isn't.

573
00:41:58,693 --> 00:42:00,997
It is indeed a little tight.

574
00:42:00,997 --> 00:42:04,693
But I think we can still achieve a lot.

575
00:42:05,460 --> 00:42:06,460
Fine.

576
00:42:09,242 --> 00:42:11,784
We're just looking today, so I won't say much.

577
00:42:11,784 --> 00:42:14,689
When you come tomorrow, dress appropriately.

578
00:42:14,689 --> 00:42:16,394
Remember your role.

579
00:42:16,394 --> 00:42:19,439
You're here to redeem yourself.

580
00:42:20,237 --> 00:42:22,589
Redeem myself for what?

581
00:42:22,589 --> 00:42:24,387
Wait...

582
00:42:24,387 --> 00:42:27,307
So tomorrow, you're not even hiring workers?

583
00:42:27,307 --> 00:42:29,372
Are you going to exploit me?

584
00:42:29,372 --> 00:42:33,380
You... At most, you're a supervisor.

585
00:42:33,380 --> 00:42:35,652
You're not good for much else.

586
00:42:37,303 --> 00:42:39,447
Fine, whatever makes you happy.

587
00:42:39,447 --> 00:42:41,457
Use me however you want.

588
00:42:43,227 --> 00:42:45,081
Close the door.

589
00:42:46,124 --> 00:42:48,284
What are you up to, Zheng You An?

590
00:42:48,867 --> 00:42:51,644
Just close it. Why so many questions?

591
00:42:55,343 --> 00:42:57,237
Are you ready?

592
00:42:58,507 --> 00:42:59,925
Ready.

593
00:43:01,507 --> 00:43:05,286
What's wrong with you? You're out of your mind.

594
00:43:06,346 --> 00:43:10,794
I'm showing you our superb light-blocking
and soundproof hotel.

595
00:43:10,794 --> 00:43:13,827
It's perfect for transit crews
to stay overnight.

596
00:43:13,827 --> 00:43:17,531
I can give Bo'ao Air a 35% discount.

597
00:43:17,531 --> 00:43:19,267
There's nothing much to see here.

598
00:43:19,267 --> 00:43:20,652
It's such a mess.

599
00:43:20,652 --> 00:43:22,387
What do you know?

600
00:43:22,387 --> 00:43:26,027
This is the best place to invest.

601
00:43:26,027 --> 00:43:28,033
What can be done here?
